{"name":"Go Alpha","hex":"#007f87","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"alpha","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The name of the first letter of the Greek alphabet (Α,  α), followed by beta. In the Latin alphabet it is the predecessor to A.","Latin alpha: the Latin letter Ɑ (minuscule: ɑ)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Designates the first in an order of precedence.","Exhibiting characteristics of the alpha male/female archetype."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alpha"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alpha","blocks":[{"text":"Alpha ALF-ə is the first letter of the Greek alphabet. In the system of Greek numerals, it has a value of one. Alpha is derived from the Phoenician letter aleph ⟨𐤀⟩, whose name comes from the West Semitic word for 'ox'. Letters that arose from alpha include the Latin letter ⟨A⟩ and the Cyrillic letter ⟨А⟩."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alpha","wikidata":"Q9887"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/K%C3%B6nigsberg_Marienkirche_-_Fenster_1a_AlphaOmega.jpg/500px-K%C3%B6nigsberg_Marienkirche_-_Fenster_1a_AlphaOmega.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/K%C3%B6nigsberg_Marienkirche_-_Fenster_1a_AlphaOmega.jpg/1280px-K%C3%B6nigsberg_Marienkirche_-_Fenster_1a_AlphaOmega.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/K%C3%B6nigsberg_Marienkirche_-_Fenster_1a_AlphaOmega.jpg/500px-K%C3%B6nigsberg_Marienkirche_-_Fenster_1a_AlphaOmega.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stained glass featuring Alpha and Omega in the Königsberg in Bayern Marienkirche [de]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AK%C3%B6nigsberg_Marienkirche_-_Fenster_1a_AlphaOmega.jpg"}],"sounds":{"alpha":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src"